## Component ①: Voice Activity Detection (VAD)

> **Selected: Silero VAD** (from Document A — not in Document B)

| Property | Detail |
|----------|--------|
| **Model** | `snakers4/silero-vad` |
| **License** | MIT ✅ |
| **Latency** | ~10-20ms per frame |
| **Hardware** | CPU only (no GPU needed) |
| **Why selected** | Prevents processing silence → saves 100-300ms per turn. Critical for phone calls where there are natural pauses. Document B's plan has no VAD, meaning every silent frame would hit STT unnecessarily. |
| **Open source** | ✅ Fully open, MIT |
| **Fine-tunable** | Not needed — works excellently out-of-box for phone audio |

> [!TIP]
> **This is the single biggest latency optimization** that Document B is missing. On a phone call with typical 40% silence, VAD saves ~40% of STT compute.

