## Component ②: Speech-to-Text (STT/ASR)

> **Selected: faster-whisper + AI4Bharat IndicWhisper** (combining both documents + research)

| Property | Detail |
|----------|--------|
| **Inference Engine** | `SYSTRAN/faster-whisper` (CTranslate2 backend) |
| **Base Model** | `ai4bharat/IndicWhisper` (Whisper fine-tuned on Indian languages) |
| **Alt Model** | `vasista22/whisper-tamil-medium` (Tamil-specific fine-tune) |
| **License** | MIT (faster-whisper) + MIT (IndicWhisper) ✅ |
| **Latency** | ~120-180ms on 6GB GPU |
| **Tamil accuracy** | Significantly better than base Whisper for Tamil accents, Tanglish code-switching |
| **VRAM** | ~1.5GB (small) / ~3GB (medium) |
| **Fine-tunable** | ✅ Yes — LoRA fine-tuning on restaurant call recordings via HuggingFace Transformers |

### Why IndicWhisper over pratilekha?

| Factor | pratilekha-v0-small (Doc B) | IndicWhisper (Selected) |
|--------|---------------------------|------------------------|
| Organization | Individual researcher | AI4Bharat (IIT Madras) — India's premier AI research lab |
| Training data | Limited Indic data | Massive curated Indian speech datasets (Kathbath, Nirantar, FLEURS) |
| Languages | ~5 Indic languages | 22 Indian languages including Tamil |
| Benchmarks | No public benchmarks | Vistaar benchmark — state-of-art results on Indian ASR |
| Community | Small | Large research community + ongoing updates |
| Tanglish support | Unknown | ✅ Trained on code-mixed speech |
| License | Unknown | MIT ✅ |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **For Tamil Nadu launch, IndicWhisper is the clear winner.** It's from IIT Madras (Tamil Nadu!), has the best Tamil benchmarks, and handles Tanglish code-switching that restaurants in Chennai/Coimbatore will naturally use.

### Future Fine-Tuning Path (from Document A)
1. Collect 100+ real restaurant call recordings
2. Measure Word Error Rate (WER) on your data
3. Fine-tune IndicWhisper with LoRA on failure cases (dish names, local accents, phone noise)
4. Keep a golden evaluation set (100-500 calls)

